# PINNForge

PINNForge designs physics-informed neural networks by running autonomous coding
agents as **blocks**: one agent, a fixed GPU-wall budget, one written summary,
in series, with knowledge compounding through the summaries. The orchestrator is
a plain Python process; whether a block is finished is a question the filesystem
answers.

Do not memorise flags. Run `pinnforge --help` or `pinnforge <cmd> --help`.

## Running blocks

```bash
pinnforge run start -t ldc -n 5        # launch
pinnforge run status ldc_5             # per-block wall, evals, summary, best
pinnforge run log ldc_5 -n 20          # scored evaluations, best first
pinnforge run show ldc_5 b03           # one block's records and summary
pinnforge run resume ldc_5             # after an interruption
pinnforge run audit ldc_5              # did any block alter another's record
pinnforge run stop ldc_5
```

Block status means: `done` (summary + budget spent + a scored eval), `short`
(usable work, stopped before the budget was spent), `interrupted`, `failed`
(nothing usable).

## Authoring a task

```bash
pinnforge task list
pinnforge task validate <name>         # 29 contract checks
pinnforge task smoke <name>            # free CPU dress rehearsal
pinnforge task anchor <name>           # the b00 score every block must beat
pinnforge task new <name> --source <dir> --prompt "..."
```

## Harnesses

```bash
pinnforge agents list
pinnforge agents doctor --ping --model <id>
```

`--ping` spends one exchange proving credentials, provider config and model id
work. Pin an exact model id, never an alias.

## Two rules

**Never write into a live `runs/<id>/`.** It is a block's workspace and is
hashed before every dispatch; an edit becomes an integrity violation.

**Never place this file, `AGENTS.md`, or `.cursor/rules/` at the root of a
PINNForge checkout.** Blocks run with `runs/<id>/` as their working directory
and CLIs walk up the tree for such files, so a copy at the project root is read
by every block and changes what a block is. Keep it in the project you drive
PINNForge *from*.
